CONTRIBUTING.md:1:# Contributing
CONTRIBUTING.md:2:
CONTRIBUTING.md:3:## Before changing the product
CONTRIBUTING.md:4:
CONTRIBUTING.md:5:1. Read `.spec/README.md` and `docs/current-state.md`.
CONTRIBUTING.md:6:2. Install the project-management tooling using `docs/project-management.md`.
CONTRIBUTING.md:7:3. Find or create the board element before implementation.
CONTRIBUTING.md:8:4. Use `task-board` for every `.task-board/` mutation; do not edit board files by
CONTRIBUTING.md:9:   hand.
CONTRIBUTING.md:10:5. Link the relevant `.spec/` documents to the task as precondition resources.
CONTRIBUTING.md:11:6. Do not implement VPN work until the generated plan has explicit user approval.
CONTRIBUTING.md:12:
CONTRIBUTING.md:13:Changes that alter protocol, security, privacy, entitlements, routing, failure
CONTRIBUTING.md:14:modes, or supported platforms must update the corresponding specification and
CONTRIBUTING.md:15:`.spec/decisions.md`.
CONTRIBUTING.md:16:
CONTRIBUTING.md:17:## Development baseline
CONTRIBUTING.md:18:
CONTRIBUTING.md:19:The current application requires macOS 14+ and Xcode 16+ with its Swift 6
CONTRIBUTING.md:20:toolchain. The package remains in Swift 5 language mode.
CONTRIBUTING.md:21:
CONTRIBUTING.md:22:```sh
CONTRIBUTING.md:23:make test
CONTRIBUTING.md:24:make app
CONTRIBUTING.md:25:```
CONTRIBUTING.md:26:
CONTRIBUTING.md:27:The planned multi-target VPN has additional gates in `.spec/validation.md`.
CONTRIBUTING.md:28:Passing current SwiftPM tests does not validate the future Network Extension.
CONTRIBUTING.md:29:
CONTRIBUTING.md:30:## Commits and pull requests
CONTRIBUTING.md:31:
CONTRIBUTING.md:32:- Keep commits focused and do not mix generated build output with source/docs.
CONTRIBUTING.md:33:- Use the configured Ivan Oparin identity and signed commits for this repository.
CONTRIBUTING.md:34:- Never commit signing certificates, App Store Connect keys, SSH private keys,
CONTRIBUTING.md:35:  passphrases, provisioning secrets, tokens, or captured user traffic.
CONTRIBUTING.md:36:- Include board element IDs and human-readable names in implementation pull
CONTRIBUTING.md:37:  request descriptions once execution begins.
CONTRIBUTING.md:38:- Report verification commands and any untested physical-device requirement.
CONTRIBUTING.md:39:- Do not add AI attribution or `Co-Authored-By` trailers.
CONTRIBUTING.md:40:
CONTRIBUTING.md:41:## Generated and local state
CONTRIBUTING.md:42:
CONTRIBUTING.md:43:`.agents/`, `.claude/`, `.codex/`, `.local/`, `.temp/`, build output, and local
CONTRIBUTING.md:44:credentials are machine-local. `.task-board/`, `.planning/`, `.spec/`, and
CONTRIBUTING.md:45:durable `.research/` evidence are source-controlled.
