codex
I found one security-sensitive edge that the current regression does not cover: GitLab release asset links are redirects and may target external URLs, while curl documents that custom headers supplied with `--header` are forwarded across `--location` redirects. Because the verifier follows the direct-asset redirect while carrying `JOB-TOKEN`, an altered link—or an unknown self-managed object-storage redirect policy—can receive the job token before checksum verification fails. I’m reproducing that behavior locally with a synthetic token and two loopback servers; no real credential or external request is involved.
